# P1: linear X.Free; X.Free; -> the 2nd Free is a double-free (warning, must-dangling)
double-free 15
# P2: reassigned between the two frees -> absent
!double-free 25
# P3: FreeAndNil then raw Free -> absent (nil-ed between)
!double-free 34
# P4: free on one if-branch only, then a common free after -> info (may-dangling)
double-free 45
# P5: single free guarded by Assigned -> absent (only one Free site)
!double-free 53
# P6: single free inside try/finally -> absent (only one Free site)
!double-free 64
# B1 -- the try body of a try..EXCEPT was emitted into the CFG twice, so a single
# Free inside it was analysed as two on one path. P7/P8/P9 are the three handler
# shapes (exits / falls through / on-clause); P10 and P11 are the controls that a
# real double free is still caught, in the try body and across the try boundary.
# P7: one free, handler exits -> absent
!double-free 77
# P8: one free, handler falls through -> absent
!double-free 90
# P9: one free, `on E: ... do` handler -> absent
!double-free 103
# P10: genuine double free INSIDE the try body -> warning at the SECOND free.
# The first free must not also be reported: that extra pair only existed because
# the duplicated body made line 116 follow itself.
double-free 117
!double-free 116
# P11: freed in the try body and again after the try -> warning at the free that
# comes second on the normal-completion path, and only there.
double-free 134
!double-free 130
